  <body>
    <main class="poster" id="poster">
      <header class="poster-header">
        <div class="university-mark" aria-label="National University of Singapore">
          <span class="mark-emblem" aria-hidden="true">N</span>
          <span class="mark-type"><strong>NUS</strong><small>NATIONAL UNIVERSITY<br />OF SINGAPORE</small></span>
        </div>
        <div class="title-block">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> CCS5209 · GROUP RESEARCH POSTER</p>
          <h1>Punggol <em>Digital District</em></h1>
          <p class="subtitle">Place, technology and the question of a shared urban future</p>
        </div>
        <div class="header-meta">
          <span>FIELD STUDY</span>
          <strong>SINGAPORE</strong>
          <small>01°24′N · 103°54′E</small>
          <button class="print-button" type="button">Print poster <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>
        </div>
      </header>

      <nav class="mode-toolbar" aria-label="Poster and presentation modes">
        <div class="mode-buttons">
          <button class="mode-button is-selected" type="button" data-mode="overview" aria-pressed="true">
            Poster overview
          </button>
          <button class="mode-button" type="button" data-mode="presentation" aria-pressed="false">
            Present 11 views <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <span class="mode-hint">Use ← → to navigate · NUS CCS5209</span>
      </nav>

      <div class="poster-overview" id="poster-overview">
      <section class="research-question" aria-labelledby="question-title">
        <div class="question-label">
          <span class="section-number">01</span>
          <h2 id="question-title">Research question</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          How does Punggol Digital District’s vision of a sustainable, digitally enabled
          urban environment reshape the relationship between
          <strong>people, place and power?</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="question-tags" aria-label="Analytical themes">
          <span>PEOPLE</span><i>×</i><span>PLANET</span><i>×</i><span>PLATFORM</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="analysis" aria-label="Three analytical lenses">
        <article class="lens-card ecology-card" id="ecology">
          <header class="lens-heading">
            <span class="section-number">02</span>
            <div>
              <span class="lens-kicker">LANDSCAPE + RESOURCES</span>
              <h2>Ecological<br />sustainability</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="lens-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </header>
          <p class="lens-lead">
            A “green” district is measured by more than landscape. It depends on
            how urban systems reduce resource use while supporting ecological function.
          </p>
          <div class="lens-detail">
            <h3>What to examine</h3>
            <p>
              Connect building design, energy and cooling, water management, shade
              and planting at district scale. Compare stated performance goals with
              observable site conditions.<a class="citation" href="#ref-1">[1]</a>
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="field-photo">
            <div class="photo-placeholder photo-green" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a field photograph of landscape, shade or water">
              <span class="photo-tag">FIELD PHOTO 01</span>
              <span class="photo-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              <strong>Add site photograph</strong>
              <small>Landscape / shade / water</small>
            </div>
            <figcaption>Replace with your field-trip photo · add location, date and photographer.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="critical-note">
            <span>!</span>
            <p><strong>Critical tension</strong> Performance claims need transparent baselines, measurable outcomes and long-term maintenance.</p>
          </div>
          <footer class="key-question"><strong>ASK</strong><span>What ecological benefits can be observed—and who experiences them?</span></footer>
        </article>

        <article class="lens-card smart-card" id="smart-city">
          <header class="lens-heading">
            <span class="section-number">03</span>
            <div>
              <span class="lens-kicker">DATA + EVERYDAY LIFE</span>
              <h2>Smart City 2.0</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="lens-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌁</span>
          </header>
          <p class="lens-lead">
            Smart-city thinking moves beyond connected infrastructure to ask how
            digital systems shape public services and daily experience.
          </p>
          <div class="lens-detail">
            <h3>What to examine</h3>
            <p>
              Trace where data is collected, how platforms interoperate, and whether
              people can understand or influence the systems affecting them. Assess
              usability alongside technical ambition.<a class="citation" href="#ref-2">[2]</a>
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="field-photo">
            <div class="photo-placeholder photo-digital" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a field photograph of digital infrastructure or public space">
              <span class="photo-tag">FIELD PHOTO 02</span>
              <span class="photo-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              <strong>Add site photograph</strong>
              <small>Public space / digital systems</small>
            </div>
            <figcaption>Replace with your field-trip photo · add location, date and photographer.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="critical-note">
            <span>!</span>
            <p><strong>Critical tension</strong> Efficiency may come with risks around privacy, surveillance, access and digital dependence.</p>
          </div>
          <footer class="key-question"><strong>ASK</strong><span>Does district technology make urban life better for everyone?</span></footer>
        </article>

        <article class="lens-card governance-card" id="governance">
          <header class="lens-heading">
            <span class="section-number">04</span>
            <div>
              <span class="lens-kicker">POWER + PARTICIPATION</span>
              <h2>Governance<br />and justice</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="lens-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◎</span>
          </header>
          <p class="lens-lead">
            Planning and management distribute benefits, responsibilities and
            decision-making power across different stakeholders.
          </p>
          <div class="lens-detail">
            <h3>What to examine</h3>
            <p>
              Identify who sets priorities, who is consulted, and which groups can
              access spaces and services. Consider how accountability and feedback
              continue beyond planning.<a class="citation" href="#ref-3">[3]</a>
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="field-photo">
            <div class="photo-placeholder photo-community" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a field photograph of people using a public space">
              <span class="photo-tag">FIELD PHOTO 03</span>
              <span class="photo-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              <strong>Add site photograph</strong>
              <small>People / access / public space</small>
            </div>
            <figcaption>Replace with your field-trip photo · add location, date and photographer.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="critical-note">
            <span>!</span>
            <p><strong>Critical tension</strong> Institutional and commercial priorities may differ from nearby communities’ needs.</p>
          </div>
          <footer class="key-question"><strong>ASK</strong><span>Who shapes the district—and who might be left out?</span></footer>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="field-trip-gallery" aria-labelledby="field-trip-gallery-title">
        <header class="gallery-heading">
          <div>
            <span class="lens-kicker">VIEW 3 · SIT FIELD VISIT</span>
            <h2 id="field-trip-gallery-title">Field-trip gallery</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Three photographs from the group field visit.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="gallery-grid">
          <figure class="field-trip-card">
            <div class="field-trip-image-slot model-slot">
              <img src="assets/PDD-visit.png" alt="PDD development model" />
            </div>
            <figcaption class="field-trip-caption">
              <strong>PHOTO 1 - PDD development model</strong>
              <p>Integrated district planning</p>
              <small>Source: Group field visit, 2026.</small>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="field-trip-card">
            <div class="field-trip-image-slot solar-slot">
              <img src="assets/Solar.png" alt="Environmental infrastructure" />
            </div>
            <figcaption class="field-trip-caption">
              <strong>PHOTO 02</strong>
              <p><b>Environmental infrastructure</b><br />Solar PV / passive cooling</p>
              <small>Source: Group field visit, 2026.</small>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="field-trip-card">
            <div class="field-trip-image-slot mobility-slot">
              <img src="assets/Bicycle.png" alt="Pedestrian and bicycle facilities" />
            </div>
            <figcaption class="field-trip-caption">
              <strong>PHOTO 03</strong>
              <p><b>Active mobility</b><br />Pedestrian spaces / bicycle parking</p>
              <small>Source: Group field visit, 2026.</small>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="synthesis" id="evaluation" aria-labelledby="synthesis-title">
        <div class="synthesis-title">
          <span class="section-number">05</span>
          <div>
            <span class="lens-kicker">INTEGRATED EVALUATION</span>
            <h2 id="synthesis-title">From smart district<br />to shared city</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="synthesis-copy">
          <p class="synthesis-lead">
            The district’s ambition is most compelling when environmental systems,
            digital infrastructure and governance reinforce one another.
          </p>
          <p>
            The promise cannot be judged by plans alone. It depends on verifiable
            outcomes, inclusive access and meaningful ways for people to shape how
            the district evolves. Test these criteria against field observations and
            cited evidence.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="recommendations">
          <h3>Recommendations</h3>
          <ol>
            <li><span>01</span><p><strong>Make outcomes verifiable.</strong> Publish district environmental indicators against clear baselines.</p></li>
            <li><span>02</span><p><strong>Design for inclusive access.</strong> Explain data use, safeguard privacy and retain non-digital service options.</p></li>
            <li><span>03</span><p><strong>Keep participation active.</strong> Let residents, workers and visitors shape public spaces and services over time.</p></li>
          </ol>
        </aside>
      </section>

