              <header class="human-development-heading">
                <h2>Smart for Whom?</h2>
                <p>Human-centred design versus demonstrated social outcomes</p>
              </header>

              <section class="human-outcome-panels" aria-label="Human-centred initiatives, intended benefits and questions for evaluation">
                <article class="human-outcome-panel">
                  <span class="human-panel-number">01</span>
                  <h3><svg class="refinement-icon heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="35" r="7"/><circle cx="37" cy="35" r="7"/><path d="m11 35 10-17 8 17H11l8-12h13l5 12M19 18h-6"/></svg>Active mobility</h3>
                  <div class="human-panel-stage">
                    <span>DESIGN / INITIATIVE</span>
                    <p>Car-light campus planning, pedestrian infrastructure and bicycle parking at SIT.</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="human-stage-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
                  <div class="human-panel-stage">
                    <span>INTENDED BENEFIT</span>
                    <p>Active mobility, healthier lifestyles and accessibility.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="human-critical-question" data-reveal-step="1">
                    <span>CRITICAL QUESTION</span>
                    <strong>Are travel behaviours actually changing?</strong>
                  </div>
                  <p class="human-panel-citation" data-reveal-step="1">Group SIT field visit (2026) · Trencher &amp; Karvonen (2019)</p>
                </article>

                <article class="human-outcome-panel">
                  <span class="human-panel-number">02</span>
                  <h3><svg class="refinement-icon heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 41S6 30 6 17a10 10 0 0 1 18-6 10 10 0 0 1 18 6c0 13-18 24-18 24Z"/></svg>Occupant well-being</h3>
                  <div class="human-panel-stage">
                    <span>DESIGN / INITIATIVE</span>
                    <p>Passive cooling, indoor environmental monitoring and hybrid ventilation introduced during the SIT field visit.</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="human-stage-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
                  <div class="human-panel-stage">
                    <span>INTENDED BENEFIT</span>
                    <p>Thermal comfort, indoor environmental quality and well-being.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="human-critical-question" data-reveal-step="2">
                    <span>CRITICAL QUESTION</span>
                    <strong>Are comfort and health outcomes improving?</strong>
                  </div>
                  <p class="human-panel-citation" data-reveal-step="2">Group SIT field visit (2026) · JTC Corporation (2024)</p>
                </article>

                <article class="human-outcome-panel">
                  <span class="human-panel-number">03</span>
                  <h3><svg class="refinement-icon heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="24" cy="13" r="6"/><circle cx="10" cy="20" r="4"/><circle cx="38" cy="20" r="4"/><path d="M12 40v-5c0-7 5-12 12-12s12 5 12 12v5H12ZM2 39v-4c0-5 3-8 8-8m36 12v-4c0-5-3-8-8-8"/></svg>Inclusive opportunities</h3>
                  <div class="human-panel-stage">
                    <span>DESIGN / INITIATIVE</span>
                    <p>PDD's decentralisation strategy brings employment and education closer to residential communities.</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="human-stage-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
                  <div class="human-panel-stage">
                    <span>INTENDED BENEFIT</span>
                    <p>Improved access to jobs, learning and amenities.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="human-critical-question" data-reveal-step="3">
                    <span>CRITICAL QUESTION</span>
                    <strong>Who actually benefits from these opportunities?</strong>
                  </div>
                  <p class="human-panel-citation" data-reveal-step="3">JTC Corporation (2024) · Urban Redevelopment Authority (2026)</p>
                </article>
              </section>

              <p class="human-development-takeaway" data-reveal-step="4">Providing human-centred infrastructure does not automatically demonstrate inclusive benefits or improved well-being.</p>
              <footer class="human-development-sources" data-reveal-step="4">Sources: Group SIT field visit (2026) · JTC Corporation (2024) · Trencher &amp; Karvonen (2019) · Urban Redevelopment Authority (2026)</footer>
