          <article class="presentation-slide" data-view="9" data-presenter="PRESENTER 3 · Hairong" hidden>
            <div class="slide-overline">
              <span>CCS5209 · URBAN SUSTAINABILITY FUTURES</span>
              <span>09 / ENVIRONMENTAL JUSTICE</span>
            </div>
            <span class="cover-brand-logo" role="img" aria-label="National University of Singapore">
              <img src="assets/NUS-logo-trimmed.jpg" alt="NUS" />
            </span>
            <div class="slide-content environmental-justice-content">
              <header class="environmental-justice-heading">
                <h2>Who Benefits, Who Decides?</h2>
                <p>Applying Schlosberg's (2007) environmental justice framework to PDD</p>
              </header>

              <section class="justice-dimensions-grid" aria-label="Four environmental justice dimensions applied to PDD">
                <article class="justice-dimension-panel" data-reveal-step="1">
                  <header class="justice-dimension-heading">
                    <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
                    <div>
                      <h3>Distribution</h3>
                      <p>Who receives the benefits?</p>
                    </div>
                  </header>
                  <div class="justice-evidence">
                    <span>PDD EVIDENCE</span>
                    <p>Planned employment and amenities may benefit surrounding communities.</p>
                    <small>JTC Corporation (2024)</small>
                  </div>
                  <p class="justice-critical-question">Who can actually access these opportunities?</p>
                </article>

                <article class="justice-dimension-panel" data-reveal-step="2">
                  <header class="justice-dimension-heading">
                    <span aria-hidden="true">◉</span>
                    <div>
                      <h3>Recognition</h3>
                      <p>Whose needs are made visible?</p>
                    </div>
                  </header>
                  <div class="justice-evidence">
                    <span>PDD EVIDENCE</span>
                    <p>Published ODP descriptions emphasise operational indicators such as energy, cooling and security.</p>
                    <small>Government Technology Agency (2026)</small>
                  </div>
                  <p class="justice-critical-question">Are well-being and everyday experiences equally assessed?</p>
                </article>

                <article class="justice-dimension-panel" data-reveal-step="3">
                  <header class="justice-dimension-heading">
                    <span aria-hidden="true">◇</span>
                    <div>
                      <h3>Capabilities</h3>
                      <p>What opportunities can people realise?</p>
                    </div>
                  </header>
                  <div class="justice-evidence">
                    <span>PDD EVIDENCE</span>
                    <p>Jobs and education are planned closer to residential communities.</p>
                    <small>JTC Corporation (2024)</small>
                  </div>
                  <p class="justice-critical-question">Can residents meaningfully benefit?</p>
                </article>

                <article class="justice-dimension-panel" data-reveal-step="4">
                  <header class="justice-dimension-heading">
                    <span aria-hidden="true">↔</span>
                    <div>
                      <h3>Participation</h3>
                      <p>Who influences decisions?</p>
                    </div>
                  </header>
                  <div class="justice-evidence">
                    <span>PDD EVIDENCE</span>
                    <p>PDD demonstrates coordinated institutional development.</p>
                    <small>Government Technology Agency (2026)</small>
                  </div>
                  <p class="justice-critical-question">How can affected groups shape priorities?</p>
                </article>
              </section>

              <p class="environmental-justice-insight" data-reveal-step="5">Governance influences not only how PDD operates, but whose needs and outcomes are recognised as sustainability priorities.</p>
              <footer class="environmental-justice-sources" data-reveal-step="5">Sources: Government Technology Agency (2026) · JTC Corporation (2024) · Meadows (2008) · Schlosberg (2007)</footer>
              <div class="slide-reveal-controls" data-reveal-controls data-reveal-total="5" aria-label="View 9 reveal controls">
                <span class="slide-reveal-progress" data-reveal-progress aria-live="polite">Step 0 of 5</span>
                <div>
